## 31. Development roadmap

Develop the software in controlled, independently testable phases.

### Phase 1 – Foundation

Create the desktop application framework, database, company master, GSTIN master, login and navigation.

### Phase 2 – Data import

Develop file import, column mapping, validation, original data preservation and control totals.

### Phase 3 – Sales and discounts

Develop sales verification, discount classification, credit notes, debit notes, e-invoice reconciliation and stock transfers.

### Phase 4 – GSTR-1

Develop official GSTR-1 table preparation, HSN summaries, document summaries and government export integration.

### Phase 5 – Purchase reconciliation

Develop purchase verification, GSTR-2B matching and IMS review.

### Phase 6 – ITC and RCM

Develop ITC eligibility, reversal, reclaim and reverse charge engines.

### Phase 7 – GSTR-3B

Develop liability calculation, ITC mapping, tax utilization, cash payment estimation and official format generation.

### Phase 8 – Complete auditing

Develop independent cross-verification, exception management, approval controls and management reports.

### Phase 9 – Government compatibility

Validate actual official Excel formats, supported JSON schemas and government utility compatibility.

### Phase 10 – Security and database management

Develop backup, restore, migration, user access restrictions and authenticated updates.

### Phase 11 – Windows deployment

Package the application, build the installer and portable edition, and test clean installations without Python or SQLite separately installed.

### Phase 12 – Production acceptance

Test multiple GSTINs, historical months, large transaction volumes and official portal compatibility with authorized company personnel.

At the end of each phase, provide working source code, test results, documentation and a list of unresolved requirements.

